pdp11-as -- the V7 PDP-11 assembler, as C
==========================================

This is the V7 Unix PDP-11 assembler translated from PDP-11 assembly into
C, so it runs host-side as a cross-assembler in the koitix toolchain.

  as1.c     pass 1, the `as' command (from as11.s..as19.s)
  as2.c     pass 2, the `as2' helper  (from as21.s..as29.s)
  as??.s    the original V7 sources -- the conformance oracle, not built
  sys.s     the syscall-number table both passes include

The translation is *faithful*: same two passes, same tables, same
behaviour and quirks as the V7 original.  The intermediate files
(/tmp/atm1a, /tmp/atm2a, /tmp/atm3a) and the output a.out (magic 0407)
are byte-identical to what the .s original produced.

Input syntax is the historical V7 `as` syntax: octal default radix,
`<...>` string delimiters, `'\e` = EOT, numeric labels (`n:`, `nf`,
`nb`), and the usual `.text`/`.data`/`.bss`/`.globl`/`.comm`/`.byte`
directives.

Build
-----

	./configure && make && make check

Pass 1 execs pass 2.  It locates `as2` at run time in this order: the
`$AS2` environment variable, a sibling of the `as` binary it was invoked
as (the build-tree case), then the compiled-in install location
(`$(libexecdir)/as2`).  This replaces the V7-native hardcoded `/lib/as2`.

See man/as.1 for the full manual page.
